# SPA fallback for Render Static Sites (same mechanism as Netlify).
# Without this, any DIRECT page load of a client-side route (an email
# verification link, a bookmarked /checkout URL, a browser refresh on
# any page other than "/") hits Render's static host before React
# Router ever runs — the host has no physical file at that path, so it
# returns its own "Not Found" page instead of your app. This routes
# every request to index.html and lets React Router take over from
# there (200, not a redirect, so the URL in the address bar is kept).
/*   /index.html   200
